                        "review": "So, after the first 30 minutes, I walked away happy with what I have experienced. I have only unlocked 2 of the 3 characters, and switching between them for combos is very satisfying. However, I think the game shines in forcing your foes into their own traps. This is highly encouraged in the beginning of the game and is a blast. I am excited to unlock the third character and unlock skills and learn combos to destroy swarms of enemies. So far, this is VERY playable for an EA title. I am not sure how many levels there will be, but all 3 heros look completely fleshed out with skills, upgrades, and they handle well. \nI adhere to the philosophy that if I get an hour per $1 spent, I think it was worth the price. For only $10 ($9 on sale now) this game will easily be worth it. They also have new heros and maps on their development schedule, so this looks like it will be a great gem in my steam inventory. Strongly recommend to those who enjoy dungeon diving and killing hordes of enemies.\nWill update when I finish what is available in its current state so others know how much content there is.\n\nUPDATE:\n\nOk, so I have unlocked the fire nymph and played her in a level. Here are my overall feelings now, after playing a bit more:\n\nSo, if you have played Agents of Mayhem or MXM, you will feel right at home with the hero switching mechanic. For those who have not, you are able to quickly switch heros with key 1, 2, or 3 as well as a roll of the mouse wheel (my fav). This is a very quick switch and is great to use in combo with  other hero's moves. I was worried at first, like I wanted to just walk around as the giant all the time, but that will just get you killed. He is SLOW as kiting is a main way of getting emenies in groups to walk into traps or do combos on. But the game does very well switching to each hero for obvious benefits.\n\nI was a bit unsure of the levels themselves at first. You can earn 3 stars on each level (like many mobile games) and those stars can currently be used to unlock \"star levels\". You get a star for completion, rescuing a goblin, and finishing the lvl in a short amount of time. I thought the time star hindered my desire to explore a bit. \n\nOnce you unlock the star for that level, you can ignore it. I also played my first \"star level\". The game allows you to skip them, but i highly suggest you play them. No time limit, a ton of mobs and traps, this is where the game feels perfect. I really enjoyed it.\n\nI also thought the leves were very easy at first. I was 3 staring each lvl my first attemp until lvl12 or 13. Then they became a bit more of a challenge. I now die here and there and I usually do not get the time star on my first run anymore. \n\nAs for loot. The game rewards chests after a lvl is completed and sometimes in the dungeon map (by completeing a certain number of lvls). These unlock, what i assume to be, cards. These are used to upgrade your heroes and their abilities aloing with gold you earn during the lvles. As the devs add heroes, i can see this being a bit more rewarding as you try to unlock more heroes as well as lvling their abilities. (you can upgrade abilities with gold if you dont want to wait for card drops).\n\nI'm currently at lvl 16 or 17. I thought the game eneded at lv 12, but further leves were to the right of my current screen (an arrow or something would have been helpful). Still really enjoying the game and new traps the game throws at me. Will continue to update as I play more.",
